//
// `data-schema` §7 rule 3 makes DDL SQL-first: `prisma/migrations/*/migration.sql`
// is the source of truth. This file is re-synced from a live database with
// `prisma db pull` and exists so the typed client matches what is really there.
// Never hand-edit a model here to change the database — write a migration.
//
// Last pulled: 2026-09-23 from the Supabase project in `ap-southeast-1`, after
// `prisma migrate deploy` applied all four migrations (PRO-68). Before that date
// this file had never been pulled and described two tables that do not exist,
// which already cost one ticket its premise (PRO-76).
//
// Two things `db pull` does not bring back, so read the SQL for them:
//
//   1. The `ml.*` consent-filtered export views. Introspecting views needs the
//      `views` preview feature; without it they are simply absent here. They are
//      the export surface, so their absence from this file means nothing.
//   2. Triggers, check constraints and the `PARTITION BY RANGE` on
//      `events.behavior_event`. Prisma prints an advisory for the constraints and
//      drops the rest; the append-only guards live only in the migrations.
//
// Event tables are append-only with a versioned payload; never mutate history in
// place, add a new row and a new `payload_version` instead.

generator client {
  provider        = "prisma-client-js"
  previewFeatures = ["partialIndexes"]
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  schemas  = ["app", "events", "identity", "ml"]
}

